Notable components:

- Citation Style Language styles and locales (data/citation), CC BY-SA 3.0, shipped
  unmodified as separate data files (Key.app/Contents/Resources/citation), not compiled
  into Key; see data/citation/NOTICE.
- The structure (item numbers, topics, order) of the PRISMA 2020, PRISMA-P and PRISMA-S
  reporting checklists, CC BY 4.0 (prisma-statement.org), used by the review tool's reporting
  views with Key's own item descriptions; exports carry the attribution.
- PDFium and its bundled libraries (vendor/pdfium), BSD-style and other permissive
  licences; see vendor/pdfium/licenses.
- hayagriva (vendor/hayagriva) and pdfium-render (vendor/pdfium-render-tile), used
  under MIT, with Key's patches under the same terms.
- opendataloader-pdf (crates/opendataloader-pdf-rs, a Rust port of version 2.0 or later),
  Apache License 2.0.
- PP-DocLayoutV3 and Snowflake Arctic Embed XS models, Apache License 2.0.
- Systematic reviews' conduct checks and AI audit (crates/key-review conduct.rs,
  ai_audit.rs) state in Key's own words what these standards expect and link to them;
  no standard's text is reproduced: Cochrane MECIR conduct standards (© Cochrane), the
  Campbell Collaboration's standards (Aloe et al. 2024, CC BY 4.0), the MAER-Net 2026
  reporting guidelines (Cook et al., J Econ Surv, CC BY 4.0; audit sample sizes) and
  TARCiS (Hirt et al. 2024, CC BY 4.0).

